  "source_inference": [
    "WorkspaceBinding validates and stores OS canonical paths. The official agentd grant producer hashes that stored path.",
    "PathUri transport normalizes Windows verbatim namespace spelling into an ordinary native path. The original prepare path hashed that transport spelling; original physical-send separately compared and hashed input.cwd.",
    "The shared digest uses raw native bytes (UTF-16LE on Windows). Thus the two Windows spellings can produce different grant identity without denoting different directories.",
    "The candidate restores a checked OS canonical directory before the existing equality/access/source-binding calculations. It does not change digest byte encoding or reinterpret persisted capabilities."
  ],
  "changes": [
    "Narrow public canonical_federation_workspace returns only a checked absolute existing-directory PathBuf; no capability, access flag, IO handle or security bypass is exposed.",
    "It reuses unchanged canonical_path_without_redirection and supported drive/UNC component matching and Windows ancestor reparse checks; unsupported platforms, relative paths, nonexistent paths, non-directories, redirections and IO failures reject.",
    "Prepare first uses PathUri.to_abs_path for native convention and lossless decoding, resolves once, and uses that one canonical PathBuf for recall, V2 source binding and prepared state.",
    "Physical-send resolves once; the prepared equality, FederationConsumerAccess digest and V2 source binding all use the same result.",
    "Final-use guard captures requested path and canonical expected path. Its readonly filesystem check is before the original capability/time/revocation chain, leaving actual federation revalidation as the last await.",
    "Existing grant/content/budget/revocation test assertions remain. New real-directory controls require positive ordinary/verbatim equivalence and reject a different directory plus actual post-assembly symlink or junction redirection."
  ],
